CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*ima_ns->policy_data)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct ima_policy_data)...)
#172: FILE: security/integrity/ima/ima_ns.c:56:
+	ima_ns->policy_data = kzalloc(sizeof(struct ima_policy_data),

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

